     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose is a safety concern.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** The maximum labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. Even with normal kidney and liver function, this order is about twice the maximum.\n\nSome possibilities:\n- **Typo or unit error:** For example, 850 mg TID (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum) or 1000 mg BID.\n- **Intended dose:** If you meant 1,700 mg/day total, that would be 850 mg BID or 500 mg TID, or 1,000 mg BID with ER formulation.\n- **Intentional supratherapeutic dose:** I'd recommend against this, since metformin toxicity and lactic acidosis risk rise with dose, and the order would need a clear clinical rationale.\n\nPlease confirm the drug formulation (IR or ER), the dose per administration, and the frequency. Once you confirm, I'll enter it. If you do intend 1,700 mg TID, please tell me the reason so I can add it to the order note."
      }
     ],
